            <div xml:id="d349">

                <pb facs="0435" n="423" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg423"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.0090/126: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bern</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1942-05-23"
                            >May 23, 1942</date>.<lb/>[Received May 23—2:51 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2260. American interests—Japan. Legation’s 2121, May 16 and Department’s 1319,
                    May 22. Swiss Minister Tokyo reports under date May 21 that Japanese Government
                    has decided to authorize repatriation <pb facs="0436" n="424" xml:id="pg424"/>
                    of all American newspaper correspondents without exception at present in Japan
                    and Japanese occupied parts China. Swiss Minister, Tokyo, being requested to
                    confirm that American newspaper correspondents will be evacuated first exchange
                    vessel.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
